# L §5.11 step 2: "A `replace rule` item belongs to the version that holds it; a `v` on it may name only that
# version and adds nothing (`LOAD-VERSION` otherwise)."  Here v names v1 from inside v2: LOAD-VERSION, L §8.3
# `replace rule <d>.<r> in <V> names version <W>`.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

def x: int at reader
  rule base = 0

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026-01..
  known 2025-12-01

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026-07..
  known 2026-06-01
  replace rule x.base v v1 = 1

ask q1: x law 2026-08-01
=== expect
refused: LOAD-VERSION replace rule x.base in v2 names version v1 ...
